{
    "background_story": "Brayan was a talented artist, but he was disinclined to pursue a career in the competitive art world. Despite his parents' and teachers' encouragement, he found the pressure to constantly produce and the emphasis on commercial success stifling. Instead, Brayan preferred to create for the sake of creation, without the burden of expectation. He spent most of his free time sketching and painting, but only for himself. His disinclination to seek fame or fortune led him to a quiet, simple life, working as a librarian and creating art in his spare time. Though his work may never be widely recognized, Brayan found happiness in the freedom to create without constraint, and his art became a true reflection of his soul.",
